# Level 25 with two players, reached by password GYLM.
#
# **What this is for is one word of WRAM.** `monster_kill_award` ends
# `LDA $20 : AND #$8000 : ASL A : ROL A : ROL A : TAX : INC $1FD4,X` -- a kill
# counter indexed by the *side* that landed the blow, already doubled. Every
# death in the corpus before this movie was player one's, and both spellings of
# zero are zero, so deleting the doubling passed every call on every input.
# PROGRESS.md has carried that as a work item for two rounds; a second player
# killing something on level 25 is the input that settles it.
#
# The prefix through frame 2084 is level25.zmv's, unchanged, plus Start on
# port 2 in the same player-select window. The tail is two box walks with fire
# held, mirrored so the two cover different ground.
#
# It works: 20 awards paid over 4700 frames, score_slot_0 6 against
# score_slot_1 18, and 00000300 / 00000900 on the two slots at frame 4600.
# The perturbation now fails at $7E:1FD5 -- the byte *between* the two counters,
# which is where an undoubled index lands.
#
# Retune by watching where it actually gets to:
#   zamn_headless <rom> shot.png 4700 -m movies\level25-2p.zmv --records 4600,4600,40
